WEBVTT

NOTE Draft cue timing follows measured scene audio and word count. Review spoken word alignment before publication.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.015
Welcome to Resgrid Academy. In this lesson, we will plan protected-data access and

00:00:06.015 --> 00:00:12.031
recovery. Sensitive content needs deliberate enrollment, controlled access, key recovery, and reviewed external

00:00:12.031 --> 00:00:18.046
disclosure paths. We will explain the features, the setup decisions, and a practical

00:00:18.046 --> 00:00:20.360
way to check the result.

00:00:20.960 --> 00:00:26.604
A co-response team enrolls so client-related notes are protected in every module that

00:00:26.604 --> 00:00:32.249
stores them. Protects sensitive incident and personnel content, with controlled disclosure and key

00:00:32.249 --> 00:00:37.893
recovery. The examples in this series use a fictional department and are teaching

00:00:37.893 --> 00:00:39.630
scenarios, not default settings.

00:00:40.230 --> 00:00:46.730
Data Protection. Protection enrollment, key recovery and access controls. Review the enrollment checklist

00:00:46.730 --> 00:00:53.230
and plan key recovery before enrolling. Availability also depends on ADP. Check access

00:00:53.230 --> 00:00:55.230
in the target department.

00:00:55.830 --> 00:01:02.157
Protected workflows. Send protected data to approved outside systems through reviewed workflows. Requires

00:01:02.157 --> 00:01:08.483
the Advanced Data Protection add-on. Enrollment is a separate step: plan two-factor sign-in

00:01:08.483 --> 00:01:14.810
and key recovery first, and review the effects on search, exports and integrations.

00:01:14.810 --> 00:01:20.650
Availability also depends on ADP, Enabled. Check access in the target department.

00:01:21.250 --> 00:01:27.787
Advanced Data Protection. The Advanced Data Protection add-on: extra encryption and controlled access

00:01:27.787 --> 00:01:34.323
for sensitive data. Buying does not enroll the department. Review MFA, recovery, migration

00:01:34.323 --> 00:01:40.860
and integration behavior; this is not a compliance certification. Availability also depends on

00:01:40.860 --> 00:01:44.380
ADP. Check access in the target department.

00:01:44.980 --> 00:01:51.557
For the training scenario, work in this order. Step 1. Confirm Advanced Data

00:01:51.557 --> 00:01:58.134
Protection access and review the enrollment checklist. Step 2. Prepare administrator MFA and

00:01:58.134 --> 00:02:04.710
department key-recovery arrangements. Step 3. Enroll through the owning screen and review supported

00:02:04.710 --> 00:02:07.240
content, search, exports, and integrations.

00:02:07.840 --> 00:02:13.327
Now verify the result. Use sample protected content to verify an authorized read,

00:02:13.327 --> 00:02:18.813
a denied read, and the approved recovery procedure. Review egress separately. A common

00:02:18.813 --> 00:02:24.300
problem to watch for: Buying the add-on does not enroll the department. Enrollment

00:02:24.300 --> 00:02:28.520
and migration behavior must be confirmed for the target release.

00:02:29.120 --> 00:02:34.490
Your practice task is simple. Document who owns enrollment, key recovery, and disclosure

00:02:34.490 --> 00:02:39.859
review. Use only synthetic protected content for the recording. Record the result, who

00:02:39.859 --> 00:02:45.229
owns the follow-up, and when it should be reviewed. Use the linked feature

00:02:45.229 --> 00:02:48.120
scripts for the detailed screen recording plan.

